{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CevJkmArheC7iiH3L2TPX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Repository findings** — what actually owns this behaviour today:\n\n- Order entity (no status field): `order/Order.kt:11-16`\n- OrderController endpoints: `order/OrderController.kt:21-45`\n- OrderRepository in-memory store: `order/OrderRepository.kt:10-27`\n- Shipment entity (already has status): `shipment/Shipment.kt:9-14`, statuses at `shipment/Shipment.kt:23-27`\n- ShipmentController endpoints: `shipment/ShipmentController.kt:26-56`\n- ShipmentRepository in-memory store: `shipment/ShipmentRepository.kt:10-27`\n- Exception handling: `api/ApiExceptions.kt:11-30` (ResourceNotFoundException, ConflictException)\n- Error codes enum: `api/ApiError.kt:31-37`\n- Global exception handler: `api/GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:13-29`\n\n**Conventions this repository already has:**\n\n1. **Exception pattern**: Controllers throw `ApiException` subclasses (ResourceNotFoundException for 404, ConflictException for 409); GlobalExceptionHandler converts them to standardized ApiError response with code, message, and fields.\n2. **Error codes**: Closed enum in `ApiError.kt`, part of public API contract.\n3. **Testing**: MockMvc tests assert both HTTP status and error envelope structure (code, message).\n4. **Repository pattern**: In-memory stores using ConcurrentHashMap; repositories provide save, findById, existsById, findAll, clear.\n5. **Request/response separation**: CreateOrderRequest separate from Order entity.\n\n**Affected files** — why each cannot be avoided:\n\n1. **Order.kt**: Must add status field (ACTIVE, CANCELLED) to domain entity.\n2. **OrderController.kt**: Must add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint and inject ShipmentRepository to query shipments.\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt**: Must add `findByOrderId(orderId)` method to query shipments for an order.\n4. **ShipmentController.kt**: Must add check in POST /shipments to reject creation for cancelled orders.\n5. **ApiError.kt**: May need error codes for the new error cases (if distinct from existing codes).\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt**: Must add tests for the new cancel endpoint and edge cases.\n\n**Risks** — what could break:\n\n1. Adding status field to Order entity changes its JSON shape; if clients are strict about the schema, they may fail.\n2. Concurrent access during cancel operation: fetching order, checking shipments, updating both could race.\n3. \"All-or-nothing\" cancellation: must ensure no partial state (e.g., order cancelled but shipments not) if a check fails.\n4. ShipmentRepository lacks `findByOrderId`; must add it without breaking existing tests.\n\n**Open questions** — none that block implementation. The ticket specifies:\n- Exactly which transitions are allowed.\n- Exact status codes for each error case.\n- Idempotency requirement for already-cancelled orders.\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt**: Add `enum class OrderStatus { ACTIVE, CANCELLED }` and `status: OrderStatus` field to Order. Set default to ACTIVE in CreateOrderRequest handling.\n\n2. **OrderController.kt**: \n   - Inject ShipmentRepository.\n   - Add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint that:\n     - Fetches the order; if missing, throw ResourceNotFoundException (404, ORDER_NOT_FOUND).\n     - If already CANCELLED, return the order (idempotent).\n     - Check all shipments for this order; if any is CONFIRMED, throw ConflictException (409, order/shipment cannot be cancelled).\n     - Set order status to CANCELLED.\n     - Set all CREATED shipments for this order to CANCELLED.\n     - Return the updated order.\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt**: Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` method to query shipments by order ID.\n\n4. **ShipmentController.kt**:\n   - Inject OrderRepository.\n   - In POST /shipments create endpoint, add check: if order is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException (409, SHIPMENT_FOR_CANCELLED_ORDER or similar).\n   - If order does not exist, proceed as before (no change).\n\n5. **ApiError.kt**: Add new error codes if needed:\n   - SHIPMENT_CONFIRMED_ORDER_CANNOT_CANCEL (or similar) for when order has confirmed shipment.\n   - SHIPMENT_FOR_CANCELLED_ORDER (or similar) for when trying to create shipment for cancelled order.\n   - Or reuse existing ORDER/SHIPMENT codes with descriptive messages.\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt**: Add tests for:\n   - Cancelling an ACTIVE order returns 200 and updated order with CANCELLED status.\n   - Cancelling a CANCELLED order again succeeds (idempotent).\n   - Cancelling an order with CONFIRMED shipment returns 409 and changes nothing.\n   - Cancelling non-existent order returns 404.\n   - Cancelling an ACTIVE order cancels all CREATED shipments.\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** (implicitly updated by changes to ShipmentController):\n   - Existing tests should still pass.\n   - May need new test for shipment creation rejection when order is CANCELLED.\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n\n- **Service layer**: Could introduce an OrderService to encapsulate cancel logic. Rejected because existing code uses controllers directly with repository injection; adding a service layer would require new files and increase scope.\n- **Separate error codes per case**: Could define many fine-grained error codes (ORDER_CANCELLED, CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT_EXISTS, etc.). Rejected to keep ErrorCode enum small and reuse existing patterns; message field conveys detail.\n- **Soft delete on shipment**: Could mark shipment as cancelled instead of updating status. Rejected because Shipment already has CANCELLED status; use it consistently.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Input | Logic | Output | Status |\n|------|-------|-------|--------|--------|\n| Cancel ACTIVE order | orderId | Fetch order → Check all shipments (reject if CONFIRMED) → Set order.status = CANCELLED, all CREATED shipments.status = CANCELLED → Save both → Return order | Order with CANCELLED status | 200 OK |\n| Cancel already CANCELLED order | orderId | Fetch order → Return as-is (idempotent) | Order with CANCELLED status | 200 OK |\n| Cancel order with CONFIRMED shipment | orderId | Fetch order → Find CONFIRMED shipment → Throw ConflictException | No changes | 409 Conflict |\n| Cancel non-existent order | orderId | Fetch order fails → Throw ResourceNotFoundException | No changes | 404 Not Found |\n| Create shipment for ACTIVE order | CreateShipmentRequest | Fetch order → order.status == ACTIVE → Create shipment | Shipment with CREATED status | 201 Created |\n| Create shipment for CANCELLED order | CreateShipmentRequest | Fetch order → order.status == CANCELLED → Throw ConflictException | No changes | 409 Conflict |\n| Create shipment for non-existent order | CreateShipmentRequest | Fetch order fails → Proceed (no check today) | Shipment created | 201 Created |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **Cancel ACTIVE order**: Create order, cancel, verify status is CANCELLED, verify shipments cancelled.\n2. **Cancel already CANCELLED**: Create order, cancel twice, verify second cancel succeeds.\n3. **Cancel with CONFIRMED shipment**: Create order, create shipment, set shipment to CONFIRMED (write directly to repo), attempt cancel, verify 409 and no state change.\n4. **Cancel non-existent order**: Attempt cancel on missing orderId, verify 404.\n5. **Create shipment for CANCELLED order**: Create and cancel order, attempt to create shipment, verify 409.\n6. **Existing order tests**: Verify they still pass (order GET, create, duplicate rejection).\n7. **Existing shipment tests**: Verify they still pass (shipment create, GET, duplicate rejection).\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the changes. Starting with the Order entity to add status:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1009,"cache_read_input_tokens":19690,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1009},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4af20350-e438-4abc-b66f-920d39404eab","uuid":"23662722-7348-44bc-8961-d0f21e243838","timestamp":"2026-09-10T19:25:42.714Z","request_id":"req_011CevJkkXAg2Ugh9PBKCxZ3"}
